# NetraPi specification documents

When editing files matched by this rule:

1. Read and follow the **netrapi-spec-sync** skill (`.cursor/skills/netrapi-spec-sync/SKILL.md`).
2. Treat **`mvs.md`** as requirements source of truth; propagate to `test.md` when requirements change.
3. Treat **`test.md`** as source for test definitions **and** current sprint section groupings; when tests change, tell the user what to update in **`test_matrix.xlsx`** (never edit the xlsx in Cursor).
4. **`resume.md`**: Section 1 = targets; Section 2 = evidence-backed work only.
5. **`decisions.md`**: process and tooling choices—do not duplicate MVS requirements here.

Before finishing, output a brief **Doc sync report** (what changed, what was reviewed, follow-ups).

Do not bulk-edit unrelated docs for typo-only changes.

## Documentation dependency map

Agent-facing overview (not user-facing project docs). Full workflow: `.cursor/skills/netrapi-spec-sync/`.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  MVS[mvs.md]
  TEST[test.md]
  MATRIX[test_matrix.xlsx]
  RESUME[resume.md]
  DEC[decisions.md]

  MVS --> TEST
  TEST --> MATRIX
  MVS -.-> RESUME
  TEST -.-> RESUME
  DEC -.-> TEST
```

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `specs/mvs.md` | Requirements (M-x.xx) |
| `specs/test.md` | Tests (TP-xx) + sprint section headers through E |
| `specs/test_matrix.xlsx` | Test status tracker (rows 16+); **user edits in Excel**—Cursor only instructs what to change |
| `specs/resume.md` | Resume bullets (S1 targets, S2 done) |
| `project_journal/decisions.md` | Process decisions |

**Removed:** `project_journal/sprint.md` — do not recreate unless the user asks.

